@startuml
title KTOB — Literary Conversation and AI Memory Approval
actor Reader
participant "Angular UI" as UI
participant "Java API" as API
participant "Privacy module" as Privacy
participant "Advisor module" as Advisor
database "Supabase Postgres" as DB
participant "AI provider" as AI
Reader -> UI : Discuss selected book / general literature
UI -> API : Send message(conversationId, text)
API -> Privacy : authenticate + check conversation ownership
Privacy --> API : verified reader + AI data permissions
API -> Advisor : append reader message
Advisor -> DB : save message
Advisor -> AI : conversation + only authorized context
AI --> Advisor : reply + optional memory candidate
Advisor -> DB : save assistant reply
Advisor --> UI : answer
opt Candidate insight identified
 Advisor -> DB : store PENDING proposal
 Advisor --> UI : unobtrusive proposal indicator
 Reader -> UI : Review pending suggestion
 alt Accept, possibly edit
  UI -> API : approve proposal(edited text)
  API -> Privacy : verify proposal ownership
  Privacy --> API : authorized
  API -> Advisor : save approved memory
  Advisor -> DB : mark APPROVED + persist memory
 else Dismiss
  UI -> API : dismiss proposal
  API -> Advisor : mark DISMISSED
  Advisor -> DB : update proposal
 end
end
opt Reader intentionally saves a reflection
 Reader -> UI : Save text to book journal
 UI -> API : Add independent journal entry
 API -> DB : save journal entry (separate from memory)
end
note over Advisor,DB
A conversation is NOT a permanent memory.
No approval is inferred from keeping chat history.
end note
@enduml
